Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:57:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(win-dshow): bulk-copy tightly packed NV12 returns

The validated return writer commonly receives tightly packed NV12 planes. Use one bulk copy per plane in that case and retain the row-wise path for padded input. The destination layout, bounds checks, metadata, and fallback semantics are unchanged.

Agent-Role: forge
Agent-Thread: /root/forge_253_tuning
Work-Unit: ZabLaboratory/Pulsar#253
Issue: 253
ADR-Revision: draft-r2-dual-lane-20260828
Evidence: exact-stride static contract; padded-stride fallback retained
---
 shared/obs-shared-memory-queue/shared-memory-queue.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shared/obs-shared-memory-queue/shared-memory-queue.c b/shared/obs-shared-memory-queue/shared-memory-queue.c
index 19601116c..77f776664 100644
--- a/shared/obs-shared-memory-queue/shared-memory-queue.c
+++ b/shared/obs-shared-memory-queue/shared-memory-queue.c
@@ -125,6 +125,16 @@ static bool queue_validate_nv12(uint32_t cx, uint32_t cy, uint8_t **data, uint32
 static void queue_copy_nv12(uint8_t *destination, uint8_t **data, const uint32_t *linesize,
 				    uint32_t cx, uint32_t cy)
 {
+	/* OBS normally supplies tightly packed NV12 to the return outputs.  Keep
+	 * the row-wise copy for padded frames, but collapse the common case to two
+	 * bulk copies without changing the validated bounds or layout. */
+	if (linesize[0] == cx && linesize[1] == cx) {
+		const size_t y_size = (size_t)cx * cy;
+		memcpy(destination, data[0], y_size);
+		memcpy(destination + y_size, data[1], y_size / 2U);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for (uint32_t row = 0; row < cy; ++row)
 		memcpy(destination + (size_t)row * cx, data[0] + (size_t)row * linesize[0], cx);
 
